NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000313 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000314 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000315 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000316 "File::HomeDir - Find your home and other directories on any platform"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000317 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000318 "=begin html"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000319 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000320 "<a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/perl5-utils/File-HomeDir\"><img src=\"https://travis-ci.org/perl5-utils/File-HomeDir.svg?branch=master\" alt=\"Travis CI\"/></a>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000321 "<a href='https://coveralls.io/github/perl5-utils/File-HomeDir?branch=master'><img src='https://coveralls.io/repos/github/perl5-utils/File-HomeDir/badge.svg?branch=master' alt='Coverage Status'/></a>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000322 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000323 "=end html"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000324 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000325 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000326 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000327 "  use File::HomeDir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000328 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000329 "  # Modern Interface (Current User)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000330 "  $home     = File::HomeDir->my_home;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000331 "  $desktop  = File::HomeDir->my_desktop;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000332 "  $docs     = File::HomeDir->my_documents;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000333 "  $music    = File::HomeDir->my_music;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000334 "  $pics     = File::HomeDir->my_pictures;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000335 "  $videos   = File::HomeDir->my_videos;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000336 "  $data     = File::HomeDir->my_data;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000337 "  $dist     = File::HomeDir->my_dist_data('File-HomeDir');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000338 "  $dist     = File::HomeDir->my_dist_config('File-HomeDir');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000339 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000340 "  # Modern Interface (Other Users)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000341 "  $home    = File::HomeDir->users_home('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000342 "  $desktop = File::HomeDir->users_desktop('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000343 "  $docs    = File::HomeDir->users_documents('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000344 "  $music   = File::HomeDir->users_music('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000345 "  $pics    = File::HomeDir->users_pictures('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000346 "  $video   = File::HomeDir->users_videos('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000347 "  $data    = File::HomeDir->users_data('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000348 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000349 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000350 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000351 "B<File::HomeDir> is a module for locating the directories that are \"owned\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000352 "by a user (typically your user) and to solve the various issues that arise"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000353 "trying to find them consistently across a wide variety of platforms."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000354 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000355 "The end result is a single API that can find your resources on any platform,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000356 "making it relatively trivial to create Perl software that works elegantly"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000357 "and correctly no matter where you run it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000359 "=head2 Platform Neutrality"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000360 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000361 "In the Unix world, many different types of data can be mixed together"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000362 "in your home directory (although on some Unix platforms this is no longer"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000363 "the case, particularly for \"desktop\"-oriented platforms)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000364 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000365 "On some non-Unix platforms, separate directories are allocated for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000366 "different types of data and have been for a long time."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000367 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000368 "When writing applications on top of B<File::HomeDir>, you should thus"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000369 "always try to use the most specific method you can. User documents should"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000370 "be saved in C<my_documents>, data that supports an application but isn't"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000371 "normally editing by the user directory should go into C<my_data>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000372 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000373 "On platforms that do not make any distinction, all these different"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000374 "methods will harmlessly degrade to the main home directory, but on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000375 "platforms that care B<File::HomeDir> will always try to Do The Right"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000376 "Thing(tm)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000377 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000378 "=head1 METHODS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000379 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000380 "Two types of methods are provided. The C<my_method> series of methods for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000381 "finding resources for the current user, and the C<users_method> (read as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000382 "\"user's method\") series for finding resources for arbitrary users."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000383 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000384 "This split is necessary, as on most platforms it is B<much> easier to find"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000385 "information about the current user compared to other users, and indeed"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000386 "on a number you cannot find out information such as C<users_desktop> at"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000387 "all, due to security restrictions."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000388 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000389 "All methods will double check (using a C<-d> test) that a directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000390 "actually exists before returning it, so you may trust in the values"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000391 "that are returned (subject to the usual caveats of race conditions of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000392 "directories being deleted at the moment between a directory being returned"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000393 "and you using it)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000394 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000395 "However, because in some cases platforms may not support the concept of home"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000396 "directories at all, any method may return C<undef> (both in scalar and list"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000397 "context) to indicate that there is no matching directory on the system."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000398 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000399 "For example, most untrusted 'nobody'-type users do not have a home"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000400 "directory. So any modules that are used in a CGI application that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000401 "at some level of recursion use your code, will result in calls to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000402 "File::HomeDir returning undef, even for a basic home() call."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000403 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000404 "=head2 my_home"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000405 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000406 "The C<my_home> method takes no arguments and returns the main home/profile"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000407 "directory for the current user."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000408 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000409 "If the distinction is important to you, the term \"current\" refers to the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000410 "real user, and not the effective user."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000411 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 "This is also the case for all of the other \"my\" methods."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if the current user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 "does not have a home directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 "=head2 my_desktop"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 "The C<my_desktop> method takes no arguments and returns the \"desktop\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "directory for the current user."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 "Due to the diversity and complexity of implementations required to deal with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 "implementing the required functionality fully and completely, the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000424 "C<my_desktop> method may or may not be implemented on each platform."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000425 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000426 "That said, I am extremely interested in code to implement C<my_desktop> on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000427 "Unix, as long as it is capable of dealing (as the Windows implementation"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000428 "does) with internationalization. It should also avoid false positive"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000429 "results by making sure it only returns the appropriate directories for the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000430 "appropriate platforms."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000431 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000432 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if the current user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000433 "does not have a desktop directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000434 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000435 "=head2 my_documents"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000436 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000437 "The C<my_documents> method takes no arguments and returns the directory (for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000438 "the current user) where the user's documents are stored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000439 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000440 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if the current user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000441 "does not have a documents directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000442 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000443 "=head2 my_music"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000444 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000445 "The C<my_music> method takes no arguments and returns the directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000446 "where the current user's music is stored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000447 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000448 "No bias is made to any particular music type or music program, rather the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000449 "concept of a directory to hold the user's music is made at the level of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000450 "underlying operating system or (at least) desktop environment."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000451 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000452 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if the current user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000453 "does not have a suitable directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000454 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000455 "=head2 my_pictures"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000456 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000457 "The C<my_pictures> method takes no arguments and returns the directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000458 "where the current user's pictures are stored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000459 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000460 "No bias is made to any particular picture type or picture program, rather the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000461 "concept of a directory to hold the user's pictures is made at the level of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000462 "underlying operating system or (at least) desktop environment."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000463 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000464 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if the current user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000465 "does not have a suitable directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000466 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000467 "=head2 my_videos"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000468 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000469 "The C<my_videos> method takes no arguments and returns the directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000470 "where the current user's videos are stored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000471 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000472 "No bias is made to any particular video type or video program, rather the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000473 "concept of a directory to hold the user's videos is made at the level of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000474 "underlying operating system or (at least) desktop environment."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000475 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000476 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if the current user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000477 "does not have a suitable directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000478 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000479 "=head2 my_data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000480 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000481 "The C<my_data> method takes no arguments and returns the directory where"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000482 "local applications should store their internal data for the current"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000483 "user."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000484 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000485 "Generally an application would create a subdirectory such as C<.foo>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000486 "beneath this directory, and store its data there. By creating your"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000487 "directory this way, you get an accurate result on the maximum number of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000488 "platforms. But see the documentation about C<my_dist_config()> or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000489 "C<my_dist_data()> below."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000490 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000491 "For example, on Unix you get C<~/.foo> and on Win32 you get"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000492 "C<~/Local Settings/Application Data/.foo>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000493 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000494 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if the current user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000495 "does not have a data directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000496 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000497 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000498 "=head2 my_dist_config"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000499 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000500 "  File::HomeDir->my_dist_config( $dist [, \\%params] );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000501 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000502 "  # For example..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000503 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000504 "  File::HomeDir->my_dist_config( 'File-HomeDir' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000505 "  File::HomeDir->my_dist_config( 'File-HomeDir', { create => 1 } );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000506 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000507 "The C<my_dist_config> method takes a distribution name as argument and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000508 "returns an application-specific directory where they should store their"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000509 "internal configuration."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000510 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000511 "The base directory will be either C<my_config> if the platform supports"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000512 "it, or C<my_documents> otherwise. The subdirectory itself will be "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000513 "C<BASE/Perl/Dist-Name>. If the base directory is the user's home directory,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000514 "C<my_dist_config> will be in C<~/.perl/Dist-Name> (and thus be hidden on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000515 "all Unixes)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000516 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000517 "The optional last argument is a hash reference to tweak the method"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000518 "behaviour. The following hash keys are recognized:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000519 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000520 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000521 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000522 "=item * create"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000523 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000524 "Passing a true value to this key will force the creation of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000525 "directory if it doesn't exist (remember that C<File::HomeDir>'s policy"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000526 "is to return C<undef> if the directory doesn't exist)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000528 "Defaults to false, meaning no automatic creation of directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000529 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000530 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000531 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000532 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000533 "=head2 my_dist_data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000534 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000535 "  File::HomeDir->my_dist_data( $dist [, \\%params] );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000536 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000537 "  # For example..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000538 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000539 "  File::HomeDir->my_dist_data( 'File-HomeDir' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000540 "  File::HomeDir->my_dist_data( 'File-HomeDir', { create => 1 } );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000541 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000542 "The C<my_dist_data> method takes a distribution name as argument and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000543 "returns an application-specific directory where they should store their"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000544 "internal data."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000545 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000546 "This directory will be of course a subdirectory of C<my_data>. Platforms"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000547 "supporting data-specific directories will use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000548 "C<DATA_DIR/perl/dist/Dist-Name> following the common"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000549 "\"DATA/vendor/application\" pattern. If the C<my_data> directory is the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000550 "user's home directory, C<my_dist_data> will be in C<~/.perl/dist/Dist-Name>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000551 "(and thus be hidden on all Unixes)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000552 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000553 "The optional last argument is a hash reference to tweak the method"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000554 "behaviour. The following hash keys are recognized:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000555 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000556 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000557 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000558 "=item * create"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000559 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000560 "Passing a true value to this key will force the creation of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000561 "directory if it doesn't exist (remember that C<File::HomeDir>'s policy"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000562 "is to return C<undef> if the directory doesn't exist)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000563 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000564 "Defaults to false, meaning no automatic creation of directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000565 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000566 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000567 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000568 "=head2 users_home"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000569 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000570 "  $home = File::HomeDir->users_home('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000571 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000572 "The C<users_home> method takes a single parameter and is used to locate the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000573 "parent home/profile directory for an identified user on the system."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000574 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000575 "While most of the time this identifier would be some form of user name,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000576 "it is permitted to vary per-platform to support user ids or UUIDs as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000577 "applicable for that platform."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000578 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000579 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if that user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000580 "does not have a home directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000581 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000582 "=head2 users_documents"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000583 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000584 "  $docs = File::HomeDir->users_documents('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000585 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000586 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if that user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000587 "does not have a documents directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000588 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000589 "=head2 users_data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000590 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000591 "  $data = File::HomeDir->users_data('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000592 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000593 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if that user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000594 "does not have a data directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000595 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000596 "=head2 users_desktop"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000597 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000598 "  $docs = File::HomeDir->users_desktop('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000599 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000600 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if that user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000601 "does not have a desktop directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000602 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000603 "=head2 users_music"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000604 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000605 "  $docs = File::HomeDir->users_music('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000606 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000607 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if that user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000608 "does not have a music directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000609 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000610 "=head2 users_pictures"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000611 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000612 "  $docs = File::HomeDir->users_pictures('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000613 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000614 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if that user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000615 "does not have a pictures directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000616 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000617 "=head2 users_videos"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000618 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000619 "  $docs = File::HomeDir->users_videos('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000620 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000621 "Returns the directory path as a string, C<undef> if that user"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000622 "does not have a videos directory, or dies on error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000623 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000624 "=head1 FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000625 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000626 "=head2 home"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000627 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000628 "  use File::HomeDir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000629 "  $home = home();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000630 "  $home = home('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000631 "  $home = File::HomeDir::home();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000632 "  $home = File::HomeDir::home('foo');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000633 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000634 "The C<home> function is exported by default and is provided for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000635 "compatibility with legacy applications. In new applications, you should"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000636 "use the newer method-based interface above."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000637 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000638 "Returns the directory path to a named user's home/profile directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000639 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000640 "If provided no parameter, returns the directory path to the current user's"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000641 "home/profile directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000642 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000643 "=head1 TO DO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000644 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000645 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000646 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000647 "=item * Add more granularity to Unix, and add support to VMS and other"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000648 "esoteric platforms, so we can consider going core."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000649 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000650 "=item * Add consistent support for users_* methods "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000651 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000652 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000653 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000654 "=head1 SUPPORT"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000655 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000656 "This module is stored in an Open Repository at the following address."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000657 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000658 "L<http://svn.ali.as/cpan/trunk/File-HomeDir>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000659 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000660 "Write access to the repository is made available automatically to any"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000661 "published CPAN author, and to most other volunteers on request."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000662 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000663 "If you are able to submit your bug report in the form of new (failing)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000664 "unit tests, or can apply your fix directly instead of submitting a patch,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000665 "you are B<strongly> encouraged to do so as the author currently maintains"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000666 "over 100 modules and it can take some time to deal with non-Critical bug"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000667 "reports or patches."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000668 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000669 "This will guarantee that your issue will be addressed in the next"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000670 "release of the module."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000671 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000672 "If you cannot provide a direct test or fix, or don't have time to do so,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000673 "then regular bug reports are still accepted and appreciated via the CPAN"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000674 "bug tracker."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000675 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000676 "L<http://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/ReportBug.html?Queue=File-HomeDir>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000677 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000678 "For other issues, for commercial enhancement or support, or to have your"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000679 "write access enabled for the repository, contact the author at the email"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000680 "address above."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000681 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000682 "=head1 ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000683 ""
